NEGATIVE-INDEX RETRIEVAL IN PAIRED-NANOROD METAMATERIALS - CONCLUSION
==========================================================================

1. Retrieval core
   Exact per-point inversion of the symmetric Fabry-Perot slab model
   (t = P(1-G^2)/(1-G^2 P^2), r = G(1-P^2)/(1-G^2 P^2), P = exp(i n k d),
   G = (Z-1)/(Z+1)).  The inversion quadratic has roots whose product is 1,
   so the physical root is unique via passivity; verified on all 756 calibration points (|P| <= 1: True).
   Phases of P are unwrapped along the native wavelength grid (m = 0 branch);
   the branch-consistency panel of retrieval_diagnostics.png shows per-step
   phase advances far below pi and a finite passivity margin, i.e. no branch
   ambiguity is exercised on this grid.

2. Compact mechanism families (wavelength-domain Lorentz oscillators)
   Per-sample free fits to the retrieved eps(lambda), mu(lambda):
     - electric_only: mean tensor-fit RMS 0.6274, 5 per-sample parameters
     - electric_magnetic_dual_resonance: mean tensor-fit RMS 0.0434, 8 per-sample parameters

3. Transfer map and model comparison
   Every family parameter is a linear function of a small geometry feature
   set (rod length L, gap, spacer thickness s, substrate index n_s), fitted
   by closed-form least squares on the retrieved parameters.  Model selection
   uses leave-one-sample-out cross validation of the full
   geometry->parameters->forward-model chain, with a parsimony rule: a
   strictly simpler family is preferred when it matches the best
   cross-validated RMSE within 10%.

